[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-007
TITLE: Bounded DC source continuation
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference engine shall offer explicit opt-in DC source stepping that scales independent-source excitation, warm-starts each stage from the last accepted MNA state, halves failed increments within validated minimum-step and stage-attempt budgets, and records accepted/rejected stage evidence. Failure at a configured bound shall be an actionable numerical failure, never a silent fallback or altered circuit.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs, src/dc.rs, src/api.rs, dotnet/Simulator.Client/Requests.cs and Results.cs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::source_continuation_records_accepted_warm_start_stages, tests/nonlinear.rs::source_continuation_reports_a_bounded_minimum_step_failure, dotnet/Simulator.Conformance/MoreChecks.cs.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF4-002
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ARCH-EQ-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-008
TITLE: Explicit regularization and dimensional convergence
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference DC and nonlinear backward-Euler Newton paths shall apply a Gmin shunt only when explicitly requested for DC, record its conductance in the result evidence, and keep nominal solves unmodified. Convergence shall require finite, dimension-aware residual and update norms: node-equation residuals use current tolerances, branch-equation residuals use voltage tolerances, and updates use the corresponding unknown dimensions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs, dotnet/Simulator.Client/Requests.cs and Results.cs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::explicit_gmin_is_applied_and_retained_in_convergence_evidence, tests/nonlinear.rs::nonlinear_backward_euler_transient_produces_finite_committed_samples and bounded diode convergence cases.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF4-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-009
TITLE: Nonlinear configured transient acceptance
STATEMENT: >>>
The configured backward-Euler nonlinear transient path shall honor validated independent-source overrides and known source breakpoints, estimate local error by nonlinear step doubling when adaptive control is selected, and commit state/RHS/time only after an accepted coarse or fine result. Unsupported nonlinear integration methods shall fail explicitly.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/configured.rs, src/sources.rs, src/newton.rs.
Verification: tests/nonlinear.rs::configured_nonlinear_transient_accepts_source_breakpoints_and_adaptive_trials.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF4-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-010
TITLE: Difficult nonlinear qualification corpus
STATEMENT: >>>
The reference nonlinear corpus shall retain bounded cases for high-bias damping, source-continuation stage reduction, invalid Gmin rejection, nonlinear source-breakpoint transient stepping and adaptive accepted-state rollback. Where an attributed ngspice fixture is representable by the bounded engine, its observable shall be compared by an explicit named oracle; unsupported upstream fixtures remain manifest-tracked rather than treated as passing.
<<<
