[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-014
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Finite nonlinear state and provider boundaries
STATEMENT: >>>
The nonlinear DC and backward-Euler paths shall reject nonfinite norms, trial/history/source vectors and malformed provider corrections without panic or false convergence. Nested continuation policies shall be validated consistently, with strictly positive Gmin reduction factors below one. DC-only recovery options shall not be silently ignored by transient or explicit-RHS entry points. Explicit-RHS policy qualification shall isolate source and Gmin continuation separately and verify refusal before provider dispatch.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived implementation requirement for the user-authorized convergence-hardening campaign; acceptance closure remains pending checkpoint evidence. Implementation: src/newton.rs. Verification: tests/continuation_hardening.rs and tests/continuation.rs. Every changed guard is to be challenged by negative/property checks and selected mutations; broad convergence and model validity are not implied.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF4-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REF4-015
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Thermal-aware coupled diode convergence qualification
STATEMENT: >>>
Newton line search shall contract the already limited MNA direction, scale diode terminal increments by validated thermal voltage and reject invalid trial candidates without accepting a nonfinite state. Coupled diode-chain and bridge-rectifier cases shall be checked across the dense LU, dense QR and faer CPU providers with independent inverse-Shockley, monotonic scalar-root, nodal-current and power oracles. Source continuation shall return nominal excitation; staged Gmin continuation shall remove its warm-start shunts before returning a final state. Any explicitly requested fixed Gmin remains separately reported.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived requirement for the user-authorized qualification campaign. Implementation: src/newton.rs. Verification: tests/continuation_hardening.rs and tests/continuation_networks.rs. Thermal-voltage stress is a mathematical parameter-domain check, not calibration of a physical temperature model. Acceptance and coverage evidence are pending checkpoint 344; no general convergence or sparse nonlinear assembly claim is inferred.
<<<
